# StudySimplify Project Rules

This document captures key patterns, preferences, and project insights to maintain consistency and best practices throughout the development process.

## Code Structure

### PHP Files
- Use standard PHP tag `<?php` at the beginning of files
- Include error reporting settings in API endpoints for debugging
- Follow a consistent pattern for database access through `getConnection()`
- Apply UTF-8 character set configuration for database connections

### JavaScript Files
- Store shared configuration in `base-url.js`
- Use localStorage for persistent session data
- Apply consistent token validation for protected pages
- Follow the pattern of checking subdomain vs main domain access

### HTML Structure
- Maintain responsive design patterns
- Include viewport meta tags for mobile compatibility
- Follow consistent header/content/footer structure
- Use consistent naming for CSS classes

## Database Patterns

### Connection Management
- Always detect environment (local vs. production) before connecting
- Apply UTF-8mb4 character set and collation for language support
- Include comprehensive error logging for connection issues
- Implement fallback mechanisms for connection failures

### Data Organization
- Use consistent naming conventions for tables (`users`, `chat_history`, etc.)
- Apply foreign key relationships between related tables
- Include created_at/updated_at timestamps in all tables
- Follow the pattern of user-to-tuition association through `tuition_class`

## Multi-Tenant Architecture

### Subdomain Handling
- Detect and validate subdomain in user authentication flows
- Load subdomain-specific branding from `/subdomain/{identifier}/`
- Apply consistent subdomain detection logic throughout the application
- Enforce domain-restricted access for users

### User Management
- Associate users with their tuition class during registration
- Validate tuition class access during login
- Maintain distinct user flows for main domain vs. subdomain users
- Apply consistent activation status checking for subdomain users

## Error Handling

### Database Errors
- Log detailed error messages including line numbers and error codes
- Implement try/catch blocks around database operations
- Apply fallback mechanisms where appropriate
- Log stack traces for debugging purposes

### User-Facing Errors
- Display appropriate error messages to users
- Implement toast notifications for transient errors
- Redirect to error pages for critical failures
- Maintain consistent error styling

## Workflow Preferences

### Development Process
- Test subdomain functionality in local environment before deployment
- Use comprehensive logging during development
- Test both local and production database connections
- Verify multi-language content rendering

### Code Organization
- Group related functionality in dedicated folders
- Apply consistent naming conventions for files
- Document complex logic with clear comments
- Maintain separation between UI and business logic 